From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:05:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 432/488] [DS4.1] Run 17 fixes: collapse decorator, packed
 merge, duck-typed batches

- mhc.py: the sink-column split left tilelang.jit on the new macro rather
  than collapse_streams, so the module failed to import.
- sink_merge: a packed row holds each rank's k values then its k indices,
  so its candidates are half its width; the merge read past the row.
- logits_rows(batch): the samplers and the sink paths take any batch with
  input ids, positions and logits indices (the sink tests' namespaces),
  gathering once a step for an InputBatch.
